<%# == Which groups of tests READ ALIKE, off the STORED census
    The suite-wide near-duplicate census (`NearDuplicateCensus`, taken at ingest by
    `Ingest::NearDuplicateCensusJob` and served to agents by `GET /api/v1/repository?near_duplicates=`)
    until now rendered on no dashboard page: a signed-in person could not see which tests read alike.

    STORED READ ONLY. `@near_duplicate_census` is `NearDuplicateCensus.stored_block_for` — one
    indexed row, a string-keyed Hash exactly as stored — and this partial renders from that Hash. It
    never asks `NearDuplicateClusters.for`, the live minutes-scale computation: an absent row is
    stated as absent, never computed on the request path.

    Unlike the per-example panels around it this one is NOT anchored on `@latest_test_run`. The
    census is repository-wide and has its own stamps — `weighed_run_id` (which run its weight figures
    were measured in) and `computed_at` — so the panel dates itself instead of borrowing the
    anchored run's date, and a reader can see when it is older than the run beside it.

    Four states, each with its own text, and the order of the checks is the point:
      (a) no stored row            — nothing was ever computed; NO numerals, because any figure here
                                     would be a census of nothing wearing the spelling of a result;
      (b) `recorded_count` is 0    — the weighed run recorded no per-example rows, so the census had
                                     nothing to read and an empty list means "nobody told us";
      (c) `clusters` is empty      — the success state: tests were read and nothing reads alike at
                                     this floor (and the sub-case of no embedded identities, which
                                     is not that claim and says so);
      (d) clusters present         — the ranking, in the stored (costliest-first) order.

    Presented for review and not as a finding of duplication — the claim boundary the "Descriptions
    this run recorded more than once" panel carries, for a stronger reason here: the floor is
    UNCALIBRATED (see `NearDuplicateClusters::SIMILARITY`), so membership is a measurement of
    similarity at a threshold nobody has validated, never a verdict that two tests are redundant.

    Outside the `manage_keys` gate, for the reason the panels around it are: read-only suite
    telemetry, nothing credential and nothing actionable. %>
<% census = @near_duplicate_census %>
<%= render UI::PanelComponent.new(title: "Groups of tests that read alike",
                                  id: "near-duplicate-clusters", class: "lg:col-span-3") do %>
  <% if census.nil? %>
    <div id="near-duplicate-clusters-none-yet">
      <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
            title: "No census yet",
            description: "No census yet — the first one is computed after the next ingest. Nothing " \
                         "has been compared, so there is nothing to show here and no count to read."
          ) %>
    </div>
  <% elsif census["recorded_count"].to_i.zero? %>
    <div id="near-duplicate-clusters-unrecorded">
      <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
            title: "This run recorded no per-example rows",
            description: "The run this census weighed recorded no per-example rows, so there were no " \
                         "tests to compare. This is not a suite where nothing reads alike — it is a " \
                         "run this panel cannot read."
          ) %>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <%# The basis, the floor and the age come BEFORE any cluster, for the reason the API block puts
        `similarity_floor` and `similarity_basis` first: a cluster count without what "alike" meant
        is a confident number over an uncalibrated threshold. %>
    <p class="text-xs text-app-muted mb-3" id="near-duplicate-clusters-basis">
      Tests are grouped by <%= census["similarity_basis"] %>: two tests are placed together when
      their descriptions score at least <%= census["similarity_floor"] %> against each other, a floor
      that has not been calibrated. Presented for review and not as a finding of duplication — tests
      that read alike can be a table-driven loop, a shared example group, or a deliberate cover of
      the same behaviour at another level, and these rows do not decide which.
    </p>
    <p class="text-xs text-app-muted mb-3" id="near-duplicate-clusters-stamp">
      Taken <%= time_ago_in_words(Time.zone.parse(census["computed_at"])) %> ago
      (<time datetime="<%= census["computed_at"] %>"><%= census["computed_at"] %></time>), weighing run
      <%= census["weighed_run_id"] %>. Stored at ingest: this page reads it and never recomputes it, so
      a census can be older than the run listed above.
    </p>
    <% if census["clusters"].empty? %>
      <% if census["identity_count"].to_i.zero? %>
        <div id="near-duplicate-clusters-unembedded">
          <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                title: "No tests have been compared yet",
                description: "This run recorded " \
                             "#{number_with_delimiter(census['recorded_count'])} " \
                             "#{'example'.pluralize(census['recorded_count'].to_i)}, but none has a " \
                             "text that could be compared yet, so an empty list here says nothing " \
                             "about whether tests read alike."
              ) %>
        </div>
      <% else %>
        <div id="near-duplicate-clusters-clear">
          <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                title: "Nothing reads alike at this floor",
                description: "SpecGuard compared " \
                             "#{number_with_delimiter(census['identity_count'])} " \
                             "#{'test'.pluralize(census['identity_count'].to_i)} and no two " \
                             "of them cleared the similarity floor, so there is no group to " \
                             "show. That is a fact about this floor and this census, not a " \
                             "guarantee about the suite."
              ) %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <p class="text-xs text-app-muted mb-3" id="near-duplicate-clusters-page">
        <% if census["truncated"] %>
          The <%= number_with_delimiter(census["clusters"].size) %> costliest of
          <%= number_with_delimiter(census["cluster_count"]) %>
          <%= "group".pluralize(census["cluster_count"].to_i) %> of tests that read alike, costliest
          first — a page of the census, not all of it.
        <% else %>
          All <%= number_with_delimiter(census["cluster_count"]) %>
          <%= "group".pluralize(census["cluster_count"].to_i) %> of tests that read alike, costliest
          first.
        <% end %>
        Each group counts its members (distinct test texts) and its examples (every run row those
        texts resolved to) separately: a table-driven loop is one member and several examples.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-4" id="near-duplicate-cluster-list">
        <% census["clusters"].each do |cluster| %>
          <li class="rounded-md border border-app-border p-3" data-near-duplicate-cluster>
            <p class="text-sm text-app-content tabular-nums">
              <%= number_with_delimiter(cluster["member_count"]) %>
              <%= "member".pluralize(cluster["member_count"].to_i) %>
              ·
              <%= number_with_delimiter(cluster["example_count"]) %>
              <%= "example".pluralize(cluster["example_count"].to_i) %>
              ·
              <%# NEVER a zero for an untimed group: `total_seconds` is nil when nothing was timed,
                  and "0.00s" would be this surface inventing the measurement it is missing. %>
              <% if cluster["total_seconds"].nil? %>
                not timed
              <% else %>
                <%= SpecObservation.humanized_duration(cluster["total_seconds"]) %>
                <% unless cluster["timed_count"].to_i == cluster["example_count"].to_i %>
                  (<%= cluster["timed_count"] %> of <%= cluster["example_count"] %> examples timed)
                <% end %>
              <% end %>
            </p>
            <p class="text-xs text-app-muted mt-1">
              matched on <%= cluster["signal_source"] %>
              <% declared_layers = cluster["layer_groups"].count { |group| group["layer"] } %>
              <% case cluster["layer_redundancy"] %>
              <% when "cross_layer" %>
                · spans <%= declared_layers %> declared <%= "layer".pluralize(declared_layers) %>
              <% when "same_layer" %>
                · one layer
              <% end %>
              <% if cluster["unobserved_members"] %>
                · lists a test the weighed run did not observe
              <% end %>
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1">
              <% cluster["members"].each do |member| %>
                <li class="font-mono text-xs text-app-content break-words">
                  <%= member["file_path"] %>:<%= member["line_number"] %>
                  <span class="font-sans"><%= member["text"] %></span>
                  <span class="text-app-muted tabular-nums">
                    (<%= number_with_delimiter(member["example_count"]) %>
                    <%= "example".pluralize(member["example_count"].to_i) %>)
                  </span>
                </li>
              <% end %>
            </ul>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
